Package: RedPsy
Type: Package
Title: Simple Psychological Network Analysis for Relational Studies
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Jose", "Ventura-Leon", email = "jventuraleon@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-2996-4244"))
Description: A small set of functions, one per step of a psychological
    network analysis. It prepares raw survey data (eligibility criteria,
    participant flow, reverse items, flat responses), builds node scores with
    descriptives and redundancy checks, estimates the network (ggmModSelect or
    EBICglasso on Spearman correlations) with node predictability, computes
    expected influence and bridge nodes, evaluates edge accuracy and centrality
    stability by bootstrap, compares networks between groups, estimates the
    sample size by simulation and runs sensitivity analyses. Nodes are defined
    with short text such as "SCS5, SCS12, SCS19". Every result prints a table
    and a plain-language reading of its key values.
